whatsie (6.1.0-1~ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Package Whatsie 6.1.0 for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.
  * Build against Ubuntu's native Qt 6.10.2 stack.
  * Lower the upstream Linux Qt build floor from 6.11 to 6.10 for Resolute.
  * Adopt the upstream 6.x Debian dependency model and application rewrite.

 -- Reaper <JohnGrimmReaper@disroot.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:03:00 +0000

whatsie (6.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Interface translations: German, Spanish, French, Italian, Portuguese
    (Brazil) and Russian, selectable in Settings → General.
  * Unread count now shown as a launcher/taskbar badge.
  * Spell check can use multiple languages at once (Settings → Advanced).
  * New Settings → Advanced option to render at the display's refresh rate.
  * Tray: centre and size the monochrome glyph correctly.
  * Wayland: match the snap-exported desktop id so the app groups correctly.

 -- Keshav Bhatt <keshavnrj@gmail.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0530

whatsie (6.0.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Spell check: fix dictionaries silently failing to load; allow adding
    languages from Settings → Advanced.
  * NVIDIA/Wayland: fall back to software rendering instead of a black screen.

 -- Keshav Bhatt <keshavnrj@gmail.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0530

whatsie (6.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drag-and-drop: show a drop hint and report files that can't be attached
    instead of failing silently.
  * Tray tooltip now reads "Whatsie".
  * Bug-report diagnostics include the CPU architecture.

